"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jupitersecho/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-20T01:14:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-20T01:14:18Z","body":"Hey all,\r\n\r\nI needed to stay on Godot 4.5.1, so I backported the iOS UIScene fix from PR #116395 and built patched iOS custom export templates. I wanted to share in case anyone else finds useful.\r\n\r\nRepo:  https://github.com/JupitersEchoDesigns/godot-4.5.1-ios-uiscene-fix\r\n\r\nRelease/templates: https://github.com/JupitersEchoDesigns/godot-4.5.1-ios-uiscene-fix/releases/tag/v4.5.1-ios-uiscene-fix-1 \r\n\r\nThis fixed the \"UIScene lifecycle will soon be required. Failure to  adopt will result in an assert in the future.\" warning for me on 4.5.1.\r\n\r\nUsage is simple. Go into your iOS export, and set the debug and release to point at the patched `godot_ios` zip. If you wish to revert, just remove the links.\r\n\r\nThis is not an official Godot release, just a focused 4.5.1 backport for anyone else blocked on the same issue.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nJupiter's Echo","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4094715425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]